.3%); Market Consistent Embedded Value at Rs 30,415 cr as of June 2026 (vs Rs 26,478 cr).","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"- Private market share at 10.1% in 3M FY'27, up 13 bps YoY from 10.0%; Total APE grew 15% vs Private industry growth of 15% and Total industry growth of 16%.\n- Ranked #1 in Customer Experience amongst Indian life insurers (vs rank 2 for last 3 years) per Hansa Research's Syndicated Life Insurance CuES 2026, with NPS of 61; maintained Rank 3 in individual sum assured.\n- 5-Yr CAGR (FY21-26) of 15% in individual new business vs 12% for total life insurance industry; AUM CAGR of 16% over 5 years, VNB CAGR of 16%, and Embedded Value CAGR of 20%.\n- Axis Bank completed infusion of Rs 381 cr into Axis Max Life, increasing its ownership by 0.98% to an overall 19.99% stake.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Recognition] Ranked #28 in this year's Great Place to Work 'Best Companies to Work For' category and accorded the Laureate honor for being among the top 100 great places to work for a decade; leadership recognized among India's Top 100 Great People Managers 2026.\n- [Regulatory] Persistency ratios are now calculated per IRDAI circular IRDAI/NL/MSTCIR/RT/93/6/2024 (dated 14 June 2024), and are reported with a one-month lag.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 13-08-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"MFSL, via Axis Max Life Insurance, positions itself as an industry-leading, digitally-powered private life insurer delivering consistent double-digit premium growth, expanding VNB margins, and AUM past Rs 2 lakh crore through a balanced proprietary-plus-bancassurance distribution model.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":0.13,"fy":"FY22","mcap":26018,"opm":2.0,"pe":102.7,"roe":8.8},{"de":0.15,"fy":"FY23","mcap":21915,